    <statement><tabular valign="middle">
<row>
<cell>The distance <m>d</m> of a point <m>P</m> to the line through points <m>A</m> and
   <m>B</m> is the length of the component of <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;AP\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> that is orthogonal to
   <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;AB\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m>, as indicated in the diagram.</cell>
<cell><IMG ALIGN="BOTTOM" BORDER="1" HEIGHT="160" SRC="/webwork2_files/tmp/anonymous/images/d87f8025-194a-39a8-925f-b6399961a0cb___0021a05c-4448-3c5d-8541-1df6cdb6d94d.gif" WIDTH="196"/></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>So the distance from <m>P = \left(5,0,-5\right)</m> to the line through the points
<m>A = \left(1,3,3\right)</m> and <m>B = \left(1,2,1\right)</m> is <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.09878</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
